WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.644 --> 00:00:20.412
took to the back of the blacksmith's shop.

2
00:00:21.453 --> 00:00:24.135
He wanted Vinnie to see the Viking swords.

3
00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:31.580
Mandy watched Old Dirk, the blacksmith, open the jewelry box.

4
00:00:32.764 --> 00:00:36.465
It was filled with bracelets, rings, and necklaces.

5
00:00:36.485 --> 00:00:39.486
"Where did those come from?"

6
00:00:40.246 --> 00:00:41.026
Mandy asked.

7
00:00:41.046 --> 00:00:49.949
"When people do not have anything else that is valuable," Dirk said, "Vikings take their gold."

8
00:00:49.969 --> 00:00:54.570
"You mean Mandy tried to calm herself.

9
00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.391
"You mean, they stole these?"

10
00:00:58.411 --> 00:01:04.301
"We Vikings take what we want," Dirk said proudly.

11
00:01:04.321 --> 00:01:07.462
"May I ask one more question?"

12
00:01:08.162 --> 00:01:08.943
said Mandy.

13
00:01:08.963 --> 00:01:12.264
"Sure," answered the blacksmith.

14
00:01:12.284 --> 00:01:15.905
"Why is the captain called Skull-Crusher?"

15
00:01:17.406 --> 00:01:18.587
Old Dirk laughed.

16
00:01:19.727 --> 00:01:26.990
"Vikings are given nicknames for their fighting skills," he explained.

17
00:01:28.191 --> 00:01:31.132
He started sorting the gold from the jewelry box.

18
00:01:32.544 --> 00:01:33.545
"What's that?"

19
00:01:34.305 --> 00:01:37.988
Mandy asked, spotting a small wooden bear carving.

20
00:01:38.008 --> 00:01:39.909
"It's so cute!"

21
00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.952
Old Dirk picked it up and looked it over.

22
00:01:43.972 --> 00:01:47.334
"Hmm. I don't know.

23
00:01:48.155 --> 00:01:50.396
It shouldn't be in here with the jewelry.

24
00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:52.918
Would you like to keep it?"

25
00:01:52.938 --> 00:01:57.861
"Yes, thank you," Mandy said with a big smile.

26
00:01:58.842 --> 00:02:01.184
She put the little bear in her pocket.

27
00:02:04.108 --> 00:02:09.711
"Gunnar, this will take a while," Old Dirk called to the boys in the back.

28
00:02:10.932 --> 00:02:12.713
He started melting the gold.

29
00:02:13.753 --> 00:02:15.494
"You'll have to come back later."

30
00:02:19.156 --> 00:02:22.798
Outside the workshop, Gunnar faced Vinnie and Mandy.

31
00:02:22.818 --> 00:02:26.720
"I don't even know your names," he said.

32
00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.861
"Oh, sorry.

33
00:02:29.322 --> 00:02:33.584
I'm Vinnie and this is my sister, Mandy," said Vinnie.

34
00:02:34.588 --> 00:02:37.589
"Strange names," Gunnar remarked.

35
00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:40.590
He shrugged and began walking away.

36
00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:48.192
"So Gunnar, how long have you been with —Vinnie paused—"with Skull-Crusher?"

37
00:02:48.212 --> 00:02:52.493
"Just one year," Gunnar replied.

38
00:02:52.513 --> 00:02:56.194
"I want to be a Viking warrior like my father.

39
00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:58.354
But he was killed.

40
00:02:59.615 --> 00:03:01.135
No one would teach me to fight.

41
00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.236
So I hid on the Sleeping Dragon.

42
00:03:05.544 --> 00:03:08.747
The captain was upset at first, but he let me stay.

43
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:10.688
Now I'm his aide!"

44
00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:17.494
Passing through Kaupang village, Mandy's view of the Vikings began to change.

45
00:03:18.775 --> 00:03:21.237
She saw many farmers and fishermen.

46
00:03:22.178 --> 00:03:24.680
So they weren't all robbers and warriors.

47
00:03:25.741 --> 00:03:28.943
In fact, they seemed just like most people.

48
00:03:31.265 --> 00:03:34.428
A group of children were playing a game on a field.

49
00:03:35.464 --> 00:03:37.265
A crowd gathered to watch.

50
00:03:38.065 --> 00:03:39.146
"What are they playing?"

51
00:03:39.826 --> 00:03:40.506
asked Vinnie.

52
00:03:40.526 --> 00:03:43.988
"Knattleikr," replied Gunnar.

53
00:03:44.888 --> 00:03:47.289
The children paused to watch for a while.

54
00:03:48.409 --> 00:03:49.590
There were two teams.

55
00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.651
Some players had wooden sticks.

56
00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:55.532
They were hitting a ball around.

57
00:03:55.552 --> 00:03:59.734
"It looks like hockey," remarked Mandy.

58
00:04:00.995 --> 00:04:03.916
Suddenly one player caught a flying ball.

59
00:04:05.108 --> 00:04:07.990
He threw it to another player who had a stick.

60
00:04:09.091 --> 00:04:10.712
His teammate hit the ball.

61
00:04:11.713 --> 00:04:14.735
But the ball flew wildly in the wrong direction.

62
00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:19.818
Konk! The ball hit Vinnie right on the head.

63
00:04:20.839 --> 00:04:22.220
He fell to the ground.

64
00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.781
His eyes were closed.

65
00:04:25.822 --> 00:04:26.883
He did not move.

66
00:04:26.903 --> 00:04:30.125
"Vinnie!" screamed Mandy.

67
00:04:31.105 --> 00:04:32.647
The crowd gathered around.

68
00:04:32.667 --> 00:04:34.608
"Is he okay?"

69
00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:36.081
asked someone.

70
00:04:36.101 --> 00:04:41.107
"Let's take him to my house," said a boy, coming forward to help.

71
00:04:42.249 --> 00:04:44.291
Gunnar and the boy picked Vinnie up.

72
00:04:45.593 --> 00:04:47.755
Mandy followed, very worried.
